@meeting crossingBackWord
// SW6 (ending writer A), the crossing back announced (ending spec, the week): Wednesday Day 31, morning. Vance comes to
// you (the Works bay, or wherever you are). Then EN2's notice, status line and his Mail (event.crossingBack.*.word).
// Two replies. Regulation numbers are Vance's habit (regulation six: shoes; nine: rest).
title: Commander Vance
from: Commander Teo Vance
gist: Vance came to find you: on Sunday at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line, and you're leading the oath.
== lines
vance: There you are. A word, Cadet. Two words. Possibly four.   [gesture]
vance > you: Sunday, 14:30, the Wren crosses back over the Line. Four weeks to the hour. The bow lounge again.
vance > you: And you'll lead the oath this time. The Captain asked for you by name. I agreed. Eventually.
vance: Cadet Bramwell is the only first-timer. Be gentle. Or don't. Tradition is unclear.   [nod]
? choice
* Me? Lead it?   flavour:share
  vance: You. You stood at the front four weeks ago. Now you stand facing the other way. That's all it is.
* I'll be there. Early.   flavour:practical
  vance: Early. Correct. Ribbons are up by 14:00. I will be checking them. Twice.   [nod]
vance: The words are on the card by the lectern. You won't need it. Nobody ever does. Carry on.
